  "term": "Kendall’s coefficient of concordance",
  "definition": "Kendall’s coefficient of concordance is a statistical measure of how much agreement there is across a group of raters or experts. In Delphi-style studies, it is used to show how consistently panel members rank or rate items, with higher values indicating stronger agreement.",
